Say why a font or a glyph did not load.

Three call sites in upstream's text path fail silently, and on a desktop that is a
reasonable choice: the font is installed, the surface converts, and a message nobody
will ever see is noise. A port inverts that. Whether the font arrived at all is the
open question, and upstream answers it with a `return 0` and one comment reading
"Pretend everything's just fine".

  - `font_load` never checks `TTF_OpenFontRW`. A size that fails to open leaves a null
    `ttf[i]`, every later `make_image_from_font` at that size returns 0, and the game
    draws no text.
  - `font_load` returns 0 for a missing file and for a failed open alike.
  - `make_image_from_font` drops a failed `TTF_RenderUTF8_Blended` on the floor, so a
    glyph that was never rendered looks exactly like one rendered and then sampled
    wrong - opposite problems with the same symptom.

This cannot live in `shim/`: the silence is inside upstream's own functions and there
is no function to supply instead. That is what makes it a patch rather than shim code.

Nothing here counts textures, draws or GL errors. oops-gl sees every one of those
without a call site and reports them itself, which is why this patch is 32 lines and
not 200.

diff --git a/share/font.c b/share/font.c
index d6807a7..3d65817 100644
--- a/share/font.c
+++ b/share/font.c
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@
 #include "common.h"
 #include "fs.h"
 
+/* The port's logging. `oops_log_*` are the SDK's own level macros over `oops_kprintf_level`;
+   there is no wrapper around them, because a wrapper would be a rename. */
+#include "oops/system.h"
+
 /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
 int font_load(struct font *ft, const char *path, int sizes[3])
@@ -42,9 +46,21 @@ int font_load(struct font *ft, const char *path, int sizes[3])
             {
                 SDL_RWseek(ft->rwops, 0, SEEK_SET);
                 ft->ttf[i] = TTF_OpenFontRW(ft->rwops, 0, sizes[i]);
+
+                /* **This return value was never checked.** A font that fails to open leaves a
+                   null `ttf[i]`, every later `make_image_from_font` at that size returns 0, and
+                   the game draws no text and says nothing - which is the shape of the bug this
+                   port has. Upstream can afford the silence because a desktop has the font; a
+                   port cannot, because the whole question is whether this one arrived. */
+                if (!ft->ttf[i])
+                    oops_log_error("font", "TTF_OpenFontRW failed at size %d for %s: %s",
+                                   sizes[i], path, TTF_GetError());
             }
             return 1;
         }
+
+        /* Likewise: the caller is told 0 and not which of the two reasons it was. */
+        oops_log_error("font", "fs_load found no %s", path);
     }
     return 0;
 }
